# Rules to follow when generating code

1. No TypeScript.
2. No JSDocs. Code should be expressive and self documenting.
3. No code comments, code should be expressive and self documenting
4. No `console.log()`.  If something needs to be visible this should be attached to the allure report using one of the functions in `test-infrastructure/capture`
5. Do not use `throw Error`. Any errors should use `chai` to cause the test to fail.
